===Etymology===
1890, from {{etyl|de}} {{term|Wurst|lang=de}} "sausage, wurst" from {{etyl|gmh}} {{term|wurst|lang=gmh}}, from {{etyl|goh}} {{term|wurst|lang=goh}}, from {{proto|gem-pro|wurstiz|something turned or twisted|lang=en}}, from {{proto|ine-pro|wert-||-d-|to turn|lang=en}}. Akin to {{etyl|osx|-}} {{term|worst|lang=osx}} "wurst", {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term|weorþan|lang=ang}} "to turn, become". More at [[worth]].

